{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the nth number in the Newman Conway sequence.\"\"\"\n\n    class NewmanConwaySequenceCalculator:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the nth number of the Newman Conway sequence using memoization.\"\"\"\n\n        def __init__(self):\n            \"\"\"Initializes the calculator with base cases for the sequence.\"\"\"\n            self._memo: dict[int, int] = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n        def calculate_nth(self, n: int) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Calculates the nth Newman Conway number using memoization.\n            It builds up the sequence iteratively from the base cases.\n            \"\"\"\n            if n in self._memo:\n                return self._memo[n]\n\n            for i in range(3, n + 1):\n                if i not in self._memo:\n                    p_i_minus_1 = self.calculate_nth(i - 1)\n                    term1_index = p_i_minus_1\n                    term2_index = i - p_i_minus_1\n                    \n                    term1_value = self.calculate_nth(term1_index)\n                    term2_value = self.calculate_nth(term2_index)\n\n                    self._memo[i] = term1_value + term2_value\n\n            return self._memo[n]\n\n    calculator = NewmanConwaySequenceCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate_nth(n)"}
