{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is undulating.\n    An undulating number's digits strictly alternate between two distinct values.\n    \"\"\"\n    digits_str = str(number)\n\n    if len(digits_str) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    first_digit = digits_str[0]\n    second_digit = digits_str[1]\n\n    if first_digit == second_digit:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(2, len(digits_str)):\n        current_digit = digits_str[i]\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            if current_digit != first_digit:\n                return False\n        else:\n            if current_digit != second_digit:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
