{"task_id": "Mbpp/104", "solution": "def sort_sublists(outer_list: list[list[str]]) -> list[list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts each sublist of strings in a given list of lists alphabetically.\n\n    Args:\n        outer_list: A list of lists, where each inner list contains strings.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list of lists with each inner list sorted alphabetically.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_outer_list = []\n    for sublist in outer_list:\n        sorted_outer_list.append(sorted(sublist))\n    return sorted_outer_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    # Handles cases where m is out of the valid range for a given n, returning 0.\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Handles the base case where m is 0 for any non-negative n.\n    if m == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Handles the base case where m is n-1 for any n >= 1.\n    if m == n - 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Applies the recurrence relation for n > 0 and 0 < m < n-1.\n    return (m + 1) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m) + (n - m) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m - 1)"}
