{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of odd-valued decimal equivalents when rotating a binary string.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_inputs(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates the binary string and rotation count, raising ValueError if invalid.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not binary_string:\n            raise ValueError(\"Binary string cannot be empty.\")\n        if not all(c in '01' for c in binary_string):\n            raise ValueError(\"Binary string must contain only '0's and '1's.\")\n        if num_rotations < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Number of rotations cannot be negative.\")\n\n    def _generate_rotation(binary_string: str, index: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Generates a single left-shifted rotation of the binary string.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not binary_string:\n            return \"\"\n        # The index represents the number of left shifts.\n        # Use modulo to handle cases where index >= len(binary_string).\n        shift_amount = index % len(binary_string)\n        return binary_string[shift_amount:] + binary_string[:shift_amount]\n\n    def _binary_to_decimal(binary_string: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Converts a binary string representation to its integer decimal equivalent.\n        \"\"\"\n        return int(binary_string, 2)\n\n    def _is_odd(decimal_value: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a given decimal integer value is odd.\n        \"\"\"\n        return decimal_value % 2 != 0\n\n    _validate_inputs(binary_string, num_rotations)\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    for i in range(num_rotations):\n        rotated_string = _generate_rotation(binary_string, i)\n        decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(rotated_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_value):\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "import collections\nfrom typing import Any, List, Set\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: List[List[Any]]) -> Set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in a given nested list.\n    Returns a set of unique elements that are present in every sub-list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return set()\n\n    common_elements = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    for sub_list in nested_list[1:]:\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(set(sub_list))\n        if not common_elements: # Optimization: if set is empty, no common elements left\n            return set()\n\n    return common_elements"}
