{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    # Transform the binary string into an integer sequence: '0' becomes 1, '1' becomes -1.\n    transformed_sequence = []\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_sequence.append(1)\n        else:  # char == '1'\n            transformed_sequence.append(-1)\n\n    # Apply Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum sum of a contiguous sub-sequence.\n    # Initialize current_max and overall_max to 0, as a difference of 0 is always possible (e.g., empty substring).\n    current_max = 0\n    overall_max = 0\n\n    for num in transformed_sequence:\n        current_max += num\n        # If current_max becomes negative, reset it to 0 as a negative sum would only decrease future sums.\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        # Update overall_max if current_max is greater.\n        overall_max = max(overall_max, current_max)\n\n    return overall_max"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "from collections import Counter\ndef max_occurrences(items: list) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n    If multiple items have the same maximum frequency, any one of them may be returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not items:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    item_counts = Counter(items)\n\n    if not item_counts:\n        raise ValueError(\"Could not count occurrences in the list.\")\n\n    most_common_item, _ = item_counts.most_common(1)[0]\n    return most_common_item"}
