{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-indexed bits of a given integer to 1.\n    Even-indexed bits are 0-indexed from the right (e.g., bit 0, bit 2, bit 4, ...).\n    \"\"\"\n    mask = 0\n    # Generate a mask with 1s at all even bit positions.\n    # The mask's effective length is determined by the input number's bit length,\n    # ensuring relevant bits up to the number's most significant bit are covered.\n    # For number = 0, bit_length() is 0, resulting in an empty range and mask remaining 0.\n    for i in range(0, number.bit_length(), 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Apply the mask using a bitwise OR operation to set the even bits to 1.\n    return number | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of sequences of length n.\n    Each element in a sequence must be a positive integer, greater than or equal to twice the previous element, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, last_element: int, m_val: int, n_val: int, memo_cache: dict) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively counts valid sequences starting from the current state (current_length, last_element).\n        Utilizes memoization to store and retrieve previously computed results.\n        \"\"\"\n        if current_length == n_val:\n            return 1\n\n        state = (current_length, last_element)\n        if state in memo_cache:\n            return memo_cache[state]\n\n        count = 0\n        # The next element must be at least twice the last_element\n        # and not exceed m_val.\n        start_next_element = 2 * last_element\n        for next_element in range(start_next_element, m_val + 1):\n            count += _count_sequences_recursive(current_length + 1, next_element, m_val, n_val, memo_cache)\n\n        memo_cache[state] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences_count = 0\n    # A sequence can start with any positive integer from 1 to m.\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_sequences_count += _count_sequences_recursive(1, first_element, m, n, memo)\n\n    return total_sequences_count"}
