{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def _longest_increasing_subsequence_sums(arr):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each index.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    dp = list(arr) # dp[i] stores the max sum of LIS ending at index i, initialized to arr[i]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + arr[i])\n    return dp\ndef _longest_decreasing_subsequence_sums(arr):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each index.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # To find the LDS starting at arr[i], we reverse the array\n    # and find the LIS ending at the corresponding element in the reversed array.\n    reversed_arr = arr[::-1]\n    lis_on_reversed = _longest_increasing_subsequence_sums(reversed_arr)\n\n    # Map LIS sums from reversed_arr back to LDS sums for the original array's order.\n    # The element arr[i] in the original array corresponds to reversed_arr[n - 1 - i].\n    # So, the LDS sum starting at arr[i] is the LIS sum ending at reversed_arr[n - 1 - i].\n    lds_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        lds_sums[i] = lis_on_reversed[n - 1 - i]\n        \n    return lds_sums\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Calculate LIS sums ending at each index\n    lis_sums = _longest_increasing_subsequence_sums(arr)\n\n    # Calculate LDS sums starting at each index\n    lds_sums = _longest_decreasing_subsequence_sums(arr)\n\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf') # Initialize to negative infinity to handle arrays with all negative numbers\n\n    # A bitonic subsequence has a peak element arr[i].\n    # Its sum is (LIS ending at arr[i]) + (LDS starting at arr[i]) - arr[i] (to avoid double counting the peak).\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
