{"task_id": "Mbpp/412", "solution": "def _is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is an even number.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\ndef remove_odd(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Removes odd numbers from a list, returning a new list with only even numbers.\"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for number in input_list:\n        if _is_even(number):\n            result_list.append(number)\n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(list_of_tuples: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum product from a list of tuples.\n    Each tuple is expected to contain two numerical elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    products = []\n    for t in list_of_tuples:\n        # Calculate the product of the two elements in each tuple\n        products.append(t[0] * t[1])\n    # Identify and return the minimum product from the calculated products\n    return min(products)"}
