{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "class Trapezium:\n    \"\"\"Represents a trapezium with two parallel bases and calculates its median length.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base1_length: float, base2_length: float):\n        \"\"\"Initializes a Trapezium object, validating that base lengths are positive numbers.\"\"\"\n        if not (isinstance(base1_length, (int, float)) and base1_length > 0):\n            raise ValueError(\"Base 1 length must be a positive number.\")\n        if not (isinstance(base2_length, (int, float)) and base2_length > 0):\n            raise ValueError(\"Base 2 length must be a positive number.\")\n\n        self._base1_length = float(base1_length)\n        self._base2_length = float(base2_length)\n\n    def calculate_median_length(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the median length of the trapezium.\"\"\"\n        return (self._base1_length + self._base2_length) / 2.0\ndef median_trapezium(base1: float, base2: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium given its two parallel base lengths.\n    It uses the Trapezium class for validation and calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    trapezium = Trapezium(base1, base2)\n    return trapezium.calculate_median_length()"}
