{"task_id": "Mbpp/441", "solution": "def validate_side_length(side_length_input: any) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if the input can be converted to a non-negative float.\n    Raises ValueError if validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        side_length = float(side_length_input)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ValueError(\"Side length must be a numeric value.\")\n\n    if side_length < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Side length must be a non-negative number.\")\n\n    return side_length\nclass Cube:\n    def __init__(self, side_length: float):\n        self._side_length = validate_side_length(side_length)\n\n    def calculate_surface_area(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Computes the surface area of the cube.\"\"\"\n        return 6 * (self._side_length ** 2)\ndef surfacearea_cube(side_length: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the surface area of a cube given its side length.\"\"\"\n    cube = Cube(side_length)\n    return cube.calculate_surface_area()"}
