{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(nums: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray.\n\n    Tracks the maximum and minimum products ending at the current position to handle negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_overall = nums[0]\n    current_max = nums[0]\n    current_min = nums[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        num = nums[i]\n\n        # If the current number is negative, multiplying it will swap\n        # the potential maximum and minimum products.\n        if num < 0:\n            current_max, current_min = current_min, current_max\n\n        current_max = max(num, current_max * num)\n        current_min = min(num, current_min * num)\n\n        max_overall = max(max_overall, current_max)\n\n    return max_overall"}
