{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\ndef expensive_items(items: List[Dict[str, Any]], n: int) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n most expensive items in a given dataset.\n    Handles edge cases where n is non-positive or exceeds the number of items.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    item_objects = [Item(name=item['name'], price=item['price']) for item in items]\n\n    item_objects.sort()\n\n    num_items_to_return = min(n, len(item_objects))\n    result_items = item_objects[:num_items_to_return]\n\n    return [{'name': item.name, 'price': item.price} for item in result_items]"}
