{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(array1: list, array2: list, k: int) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Finds the kth smallest element from two given sorted arrays.\n    Raises IndexError if k is out of bounds (not positive or exceeds total length).\"\"\"\n    m, n = len(array1), len(array2)\n\n    # Validate k: it must be a positive integer and within the combined length of arrays.\n    if k <= 0 or k > (m + n):\n        raise IndexError(\"k is out of bounds or not a positive integer.\")\n\n    p1 = 0  # Pointer for array1\n    p2 = 0  # Pointer for array2\n    kth_element = None\n\n    # Iterate k times, finding the smallest element at each step, until the k-th element is found.\n    while k > 0:\n        k -= 1\n\n        # If array1 is exhausted, take the next element from array2.\n        if p1 == m:\n            kth_element = array2[p2]\n            p2 += 1\n            continue\n\n        # If array2 is exhausted, take the next element from array1.\n        if p2 == n:\n            kth_element = array1[p1]\n            p1 += 1\n            continue\n\n        # Compare elements from both arrays and pick the smaller one.\n        if array1[p1] <= array2[p2]:\n            kth_element = array1[p1]\n            p1 += 1\n        else:\n            kth_element = array2[p2]\n            p2 += 1\n            \n    return kth_element"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "def sum_average(n: int) -> tuple[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum and average of the first n natural numbers.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Calculate sum using the formula n * (n + 1) / 2\n    total_sum = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    # Calculate average\n    average = total_sum / n\n\n    return (total_sum, average)"}
