{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "def tuple_modulo(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs an element-wise modulo operation on two tuples of the same length.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input tuples are not of the same length.\n        ZeroDivisionError: If any element in tuple2 is zero, leading to a modulo by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if tuple2[i] == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Modulo by zero encountered.\")\n        results.append(tuple1[i] % tuple2[i])\n    return tuple(results)"}
