{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _is_divisible_subset(subset: List[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if every pair of numbers in the subset satisfies the divisibility rule.\n    Assumes all numbers in the subset are positive integers.\"\"\"\n    if len(subset) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    n = len(subset)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            num1 = subset[i]\n            num2 = subset[j]\n            # For a pair (num1, num2) to be divisible, num1 must divide num2 or vice-versa.\n            if not (num1 % num2 == 0 or num2 % num1 == 0):\n                return False\n    return True\ndef _generate_subsets(numbers: List[int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"Recursively generates all possible subsets (power set) of a list of numbers.\"\"\"\n    all_subsets = []\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    def backtrack(index: int, current_subset: List[int]):\n        all_subsets.append(list(current_subset)) # Add a copy of the current subset\n\n        for i in range(index, n):\n            current_subset.append(numbers[i])\n            backtrack(i + 1, current_subset)\n            current_subset.pop() # Backtrack to explore other possibilities\n\n    backtrack(0, [])\n    return all_subsets\ndef largest_subset(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of a list of numbers so that every pair is divisible.\n    A pair (a, b) is divisible if a % b == 0 or b % a == 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle specific edge cases for input list as per design context\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n    if len(numbers) == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    all_subsets = _generate_subsets(numbers)\n    \n    max_size = 0\n    # Iterate through all generated subsets to find the largest divisible one.\n    for subset in all_subsets:\n        if _is_divisible_subset(subset):\n            max_size = max(max_size, len(subset))\n            \n    return max_size"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "solution": "def move_num(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Moves all numeric characters to the end of the given string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string: The string to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        The processed string with all numbers moved to the end.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_numeric_chars = []\n    numeric_chars = []\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            numeric_chars.append(char)\n        else:\n            non_numeric_chars.append(char)\n\n    return ''.join(non_numeric_chars) + ''.join(numeric_chars)"}
