{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It iterates through both lists to find the two middle elements of the merged list.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n    m1 = -1 # To store the (n-1)-th element (0-indexed)\n    m2 = -1 # To store the n-th element (0-indexed)\n\n    # Iterate to find the n-th and (n+1)-th elements of the merged list\n    # (which are at 0-indexed positions n-1 and n)\n    for count in range(n + 1):\n        if i == n: # list1 exhausted\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n: # list2 exhausted\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
