{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "import math\nclass Cell:\n    \"\"\"Represents a single cell in the matrix with its coordinates and cost.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, row: int, column: int, cost: int):\n        self.row = row\n        self.column = column\n        self.cost = cost\nclass Path:\n    \"\"\"Manages a sequence of cells forming a path and calculates its metrics.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, initial_cell: Cell):\n        self.cells_in_path = [initial_cell]\n        self.total_cost = float(initial_cell.cost)\n        self.number_of_cells = 1\n        self.average = float(initial_cell.cost)\n\n    def add_cell(self, cell: Cell):\n        self.cells_in_path.append(cell)\n        self.total_cost += cell.cost\n        self.number_of_cells += 1\n\n    def remove_last_cell(self):\n        removed_cell = self.cells_in_path.pop()\n        self.total_cost -= removed_cell.cost\n        self.number_of_cells -= 1\n        self.calculate_metrics() # Recalculate average after removal\n\n    def calculate_metrics(self):\n        if self.number_of_cells > 0:\n            self.average = self.total_cost / self.number_of_cells\n        else:\n            self.average = 0.0 # Should not happen in this problem context\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates finding all valid paths, calculating their averages, and returning the maximum average.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n    all_paths = []\n\n    def _find_all_paths_dfs(matrix: list[list[int]], current_row: int, current_col: int, current_path: Path, all_paths: list[Path], N: int):\n        # If we reached the bottom-right cell, this path is complete\n        if current_row == N - 1 and current_col == N - 1:\n            # We need to store a copy of the path, not the reference\n            path_copy = Path(current_path.cells_in_path[0])\n            for i in range(1, len(current_path.cells_in_path)):\n                path_copy.add_cell(current_path.cells_in_path[i])\n            path_copy.calculate_metrics()\n            all_paths.append(path_copy)\n            return\n\n        # Move right\n        if current_col + 1 < N:\n            next_cell = Cell(current_row, current_col + 1, matrix[current_row][current_col + 1])\n            current_path.add_cell(next_cell)\n            _find_all_paths_dfs(matrix, current_row, current_col + 1, current_path, all_paths, N)\n            current_path.remove_last_cell() # Backtrack\n\n        # Move down\n        if current_row + 1 < N:\n            next_cell = Cell(current_row + 1, current_col, matrix[current_row + 1][current_col])\n            current_path.add_cell(next_cell)\n            _find_all_paths_dfs(matrix, current_row + 1, current_col, current_path, all_paths, N)\n            current_path.remove_last_cell() # Backtrack\n\n    initial_cell = Cell(0, 0, matrix[0][0])\n    current_path_instance = Path(initial_cell)\n    _find_all_paths_dfs(matrix, 0, 0, current_path_instance, all_paths, N)\n\n    max_average = -math.inf\n    for path in all_paths:\n        if path.average > max_average:\n            max_average = path.average\n\n    return max_average"}
