{"task_id": "Mbpp/728", "solution": "def sum_list(list_A: list[float | int], list_B: list[float | int]) -> list[float | int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the element-wise sum of two lists of numbers.\n\n    Raises ValueError if list_A and list_B are not of equal length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list_A) != len(list_B):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must be of equal length for element-wise summation.\")\n\n    result_list = []\n    for i in range(len(list_A)):\n        result_list.append(list_A[i] + list_B[i])\n    return result_list"}
